Rust dependencies with embedded data
------------------------------------
- `kakasi` 0.1.0 (GPL-3.0): Japanese kanji/kana readings; its 1.4 MiB dictionary
  is compiled into the binary. The crate is a port of pykakasi
  (Copyright (C) 2010-2021 Hiroshi Miura and contributors), whose dictionaries
  come from the original kakasi project (GPL-2.0, Copyright (C) 1992-1994
  Hironobu Takahashi and others). The crate is licensed GPL-3.0 (only), the same
  licence as this project, so the combined work stays GPL-3.0-only and the text
  in LICENSE covers it.
- `pinyin` 0.11.0 (MIT): Hanzi → pinyin table from mozillazg/pinyin-data (MIT).

Bundled audio backend
---------------------
The AppImage bundles mpv 0.35.1 and its non-system shared libraries under
usr/lib/metrolist/mpv/. mpv is licensed GPL-2.0-or-later; the Debian bookworm
build's FFmpeg libraries are LGPL-2.1-or-later, libass is ISC, and libplacebo
is LGPL-2.1-or-later. Copyright files and a generated PROVENANCE.txt are in
usr/share/licenses/metrolist-desktop/mpv/. Additional bundled libraries (codec
and container libraries pulled in by FFmpeg) keep their Debian package
copyright files in the same directory.

Source: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv (mpv)
        https://ffmpeg.org/ (FFmpeg)
        https://github.com/libass/libass (libass)
        https://code.videolan.org/videolan/libplacebo (libplacebo)

The host's mpv 0.41 is not used in the released AppImage: it requires
GLIBC_2.38 and FFmpeg 7, while this AppImage targets the Debian 12/Ubuntu 24.04
GLIBC_2.36 floor. The bundled mpv is a separate executable, not linked into
Metrolist; the app talks to it over its JSON IPC socket.

